From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Continue: the phone lip card, the drawer list, pending app
 switcher cards and the TV home hero (ADR-055 Phase C)

Phone and tablet: the Continue offer is the lip card; Continue turns it into
"Opening <app> from <device>" in place (the Connect badge drops, the card is
not replaced), and the result list is a bottom drawer. The source device's
other apps wait in the app switcher as pending cards (icon, no picture) until
chosen; swiping one away forgets it.

TV: no prompt. The home's hero shows what was playing on another device: the
app and "From <device>" chips, the item, minutes left, Continue (focused) and
Start over, over the item's artwork under the home's shade. lumaSession
sends the artwork as a JPEG of at most 96 KB made from the player's local
cover art (file:// only; a remote URL is never fetched).

Apps the other device has and this one doesn't show the name and icon from
Depot's catalogue and media cache, for the host Depot and the Depot Flatpak.

Tablet: the phone shell with room. The lip card is the phone's (340), and
the result list is the phone's drawer, 400 wide, centred and 16 px above the
foot with all corners round. The card's choices take equal shares of the
row, and a card without buttons keeps no room for them.

